# Express API

- Keep routes thin: validate input → do work → return JSON.
- Use `express.json()` when accepting JSON bodies.
- Prefer small modules (`routes/`, helpers) when `index.js` grows; do not over-engineer early.
- Use environment variables for config (`process.env.PORT`, etc.); never hardcode secrets.
- Keep `/health` working — the frontend uses it for local checks.
- Log useful startup and error messages; never log passwords or tokens.
- Do not block the event loop with heavy sync work in request handlers.
- Export the app or keep listen logic clear so routes stay easy to find.
